  "thumbnailAlt": "Customer Feedback form beside a photo of two customers chatting with a barista at a cafe counter",
  "content": {
    "intro": "A customer feedback form is a form that collects a customer's overall rating, what they liked, what disappointed them and whether they would come back, so a business can fix problems and repeat what works. This template pairs quick rating questions with two open text boxes, so you get numbers to track and the reasons behind them.",
    "audience": "Shops, cafes, salons, agencies, online stores and service businesses that want honest feedback after a purchase or visit.",
    "useCases": [
      "A QR code on receipts or table cards after a meal or visit",
      "A link in the order-delivered email from an online store",
      "Feedback after a completed service job, such as a repair or cleaning",
      "Checking how a new product, menu or opening hours land with regulars"
    ],
    "tips": [
      "Use conditional logic to show the 'What went wrong?' box only when someone rates 1 or 2, so happy customers finish faster.",
      "Turn on email notifications so a manager sees low scores the same day and can reply while the customer still cares.",
      "Open the per-question charts in response analytics each month to see if your average rating is moving."
    ],
    "faq": [
      {
        "question": "What should a customer feedback form include?",
        "answer": "An overall satisfaction rating, a few ratings on specific things (quality, speed, staff, value), an open question about what went well, an open question about what to improve, a repeat or recommend question, and optional contact details with permission to follow up."
      },
      {
        "question": "How long should a customer feedback form be?",
        "answer": "Short enough to finish in under two minutes. Six to ten questions with mostly taps and one or two text boxes keeps completion rates high."
      },
      {
        "question": "Should customer feedback be anonymous?",
        "answer": "Give people the choice. This template makes name and email optional and asks for permission before you contact anyone, which tends to produce more honest answers."
      },
      {
        "question": "When is the best time to ask for customer feedback?",
        "answer": "Right after the experience, while it is fresh: at the table, at checkout, or within a day of delivery or service. Feedback gathered weeks later is vaguer and less useful."
      }
    ]
  },
